nels from 1,243 to 1,099 MiB. All hidden states and final features matched bitwise in both modes.", "With resident weights, loading ViT-H+ on an RTX 5060 Ti peaked at 1,604 MiB allocated in CUDA portable mode after host-side packing. The prior loader peaked at 6,542 MiB. Both produced bit-identical reference outputs.", "CUDA portable and kernels accept stream=True to stage packed transformer blocks from pinned host RAM. This setting uses eager inference. Export and CUDA graph replay require resident weights.", "kernels replays a CUDA graph per small input shape and layer set (up to 512 px, ViT-S 1024 px), captured on the shape's second call; at most 8 per model holding at most 256 MB of outputs (a full cache replaces only graphs unused for 64 calls, other new shapes run eagerly).", "The graphs' shared memory pool (intermediates) comes on top of that limit and stays reserved: up to about 470 MB more PyTorch cache than eager for ViT-H+ at 512 px with all layers, usually under 75 MB; `model.release_graphs()` frees it on the device."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: dense patch features and a pooled image feature.", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "dinov3-vits16", "released": "0.3.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "dinov3-vits16@1", "name": "dinov3-vits16", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {"arch": "vits16"}, "licence": {"code": "LicenseRef-DINOv3-License", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "LicenseRef-DINOv3-License", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vits16-pretrain-lvd1689m/blob/114c1379950215c8b35dfcd4e90a5c251dde0d32/LICENSE.md (DINOv3 License, the same file in every model repo; gated: accept on Hugging Face to download)", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "LVD-1689M: 1.689B images curated from 17B public Instagram images by retrieval / clustering, self-supervised (no labels), per the paper; n